           <i> every day</i>


01:02:23.340 --> 01:02:27.442
      <i> and they're not used</i>
     <i> to repetitive motions</i>


01:02:27.444 --> 01:02:29.945
       <i> in their actions.</i>


01:02:29.947 --> 01:02:32.080
    It can be kind of tiring


01:02:32.082 --> 01:02:33.448
           just to do
    the same thing every day


01:02:33.450 --> 01:02:35.283
     You have to bring some
         spice into it.


01:02:42.125 --> 01:02:43.325
           <i> Thank you.</i>


01:02:47.930 --> 01:02:51.533
            Francis,
     your chef at McMurdo,


01:02:52.902 --> 01:02:55.036
       we exchange a few.


01:02:56.873 --> 01:02:59.040
      He brought his mead


01:02:59.042 --> 01:03:01.543
    and I gave him a bottle,


01:03:01.545 --> 01:03:03.345
    this mixed nine bottle.


01:03:03.347 --> 01:03:05.514
    And he says it's a very
          good drink.


01:03:05.516 --> 01:03:08.250
            So well,
    tell me what you think?


01:03:08.252 --> 01:03:10.118
           - Cheers.
           -<i> L'chaim.</i>


01:03:13.356 --> 01:03:16.491
   <i> The winter season sets up</i>
        <i> and offers more</i>


01:03:16.493 --> 01:03:18.527
<i>of an introspective outlook...</i>


01:03:20.563 --> 01:03:22.964
         <i> where you can</i>
     <i> take the time to read</i>


01:03:22.966 --> 01:03:24.232
      <i> or work on a craft.</i>


01:03:25.501 --> 01:03:26.535
      <i> There's still times</i>


01:03:26.537 --> 01:03:30.138
  <i> But I think it really helps</i>


01:03:30.140 --> 01:03:32.007
           <i> if you can</i>
     <i> spend that time alone.</i>


01:03:34.377 --> 01:03:38.313
 <i> There's no substitute for just</i>
<i>having a good book in your hand.</i>


01:03:38.315 --> 01:03:40.248
          Andrew Weil.


01:03:40.250 --> 01:03:43.351
     Now it's a very small
       small print here.


01:03:43.353 --> 01:03:44.586
        Biblical Hebrew.


01:03:44.588 --> 01:03:46.988
  Grammar of biblical Hebrew.


01:03:46.990 --> 01:03:48.957
            <i> I knit.</i>


01:03:48.959 --> 01:03:51.993
   <i> It keeps away the feeling</i>
<i>of stir craziness in the winter</i>


01:03:51.995 --> 01:03:54.329
 <i> when I just feel like I might</i>
    <i> like to tear my hair out</i>


01:03:54.331 --> 01:03:55.330
   <i> and run outside screaming.</i>


01:04:51.153 --> 01:04:52.420
   <i> Towards the end of winter</i>


01:04:52.422 --> 01:04:54.556
       <i> the extreme cold,</i>
          <i> the fatigue,</i>


01:04:54.558 --> 01:04:57.926
 <i> and constant lack of sunlight</i>
      <i> or any new stimulus</i>


01:04:57.928 --> 01:05:01.196
      <i> creates a condition</i>
      <i> called T3 Syndrome.</i>


01:05:01.198 --> 01:05:03.031
    <i> Attention all stations,</i>


01:05:03.033 --> 01:05:04.466
  <i> standby for a severe weather</i>
    <i> condition announcement.</i>


01:05:04.468 --> 01:05:05.967
          <i> The N-S-S--</i>


01:05:07.303 --> 01:05:09.471
     <i> N-S-F station manager,</i>


01:05:09.473 --> 01:05:12.207
     <i> has set severe weather</i>
      <i> condition one for...</i>


01:05:14.043 --> 01:05:16.077
    <i> the following locations.</i>


01:05:16.079 --> 01:05:17.345
    <i> So I work at the store,</i>


01:05:17.347 --> 01:05:19.648
<i>and we open every day at 11:30,</i>


01:05:19.650 --> 01:05:21.483
      <i> and almost every day</i>


01:05:21.485 --> 01:05:22.651
      <i> this person comes in</i>


01:05:22.653 --> 01:05:26.254
   <i> and buys something at like</i>
        <i> 11:35 or 11:40.</i>


01:05:26.256 --> 01:05:27.188
 <i> We have the same conversation.</i>


01:05:27.190 --> 01:05:31.960
       <i> I usually give him</i>
     <i> a pack of cigarettes.</i>


01:05:31.962 --> 01:05:33.495
       <i> And the other day</i>
     <i> at about the same time</i>


01:05:33.497 --> 01:05:35.463
          <i> he comes in</i>
       <i> and he goes "Wow!</i>


01:05:35.465 --> 01:05:37.432
         I didn't know
 you guys opened at this time.


01:05:37.434 --> 01:05:39.334
   Have you always been open
         at this time?"


01:05:39.336 --> 01:05:40.936
        And I was like,


01:05:40.938 --> 01:05:43.271
          "So and so,
 you come in every single day.


01:05:43.273 --> 01:05:46.174
     You buy the same thing
       every single day."


01:05:46.176 --> 01:05:47.142
     And he was just like,


01:05:47.144 --> 01:05:49.244
 "Wow, I never thought you guys
    were open at this time."


01:05:49.246 --> 01:05:51.012
      and he just kind of
         wandered off.


01:05:55.618 --> 01:05:57.385
     Firehouse, Genevieve.


01:05:57.987 --> 01:06:00.989
      <i> A couple of days ago</i>
    <i> Talie called and I said</i>


01:06:00.991 --> 01:06:01.957
          <i> "Oh, Talie,</i>
    <i> I'm so glad you called.</i>


01:06:01.959 --> 01:06:04.559
  <i> I was just thinking about...</i>
   <i> I was thinking about you.</i>


01:06:04.561 --> 01:06:05.961
 <i> I was just about to page you."</i>


01:06:05.963 --> 01:06:06.995
         <i> And she said,</i>
    <i> "Well you did page me."</i>


01:06:06.997 --> 01:06:10.031
 So I had completely forgotten
     that I had paged her.


01:06:10.033 --> 01:06:12.600
    And that seems to happen
      more times than not.


01:06:12.602 --> 01:06:15.603
   <i> There was a time where...</i>
   <i> I was... had to go outside</i>


01:06:15.605 --> 01:06:19.240
       <i> and the chief she</i>
  <i> tossed down a pair of boots.</i>


01:06:19.242 --> 01:06:21.276
           <i> I go ahead</i>
       <i> and I put them on</i>


01:06:21.278 --> 01:06:23.044
 <i> and I'm walking around in them</i>


01:06:23.046 --> 01:06:24.412
    they feel really weird.


01:06:25.314 --> 01:06:26.548
       I don't know why.


01:06:26.550 --> 01:06:29.150
  I get to the door of the bay


01:06:29.152 --> 01:06:31.319
    where I'm leaving and...


01:06:31.321 --> 01:06:32.287
     and I look down and...


01:06:32.289 --> 01:06:34.456
   they're on the wrong feet.


01:06:34.458 --> 01:06:37.025
        So I walk back,
        I pull them off.


01:06:37.027 --> 01:06:39.761
   I take the right boot off
        and set it down.


01:06:39.763 --> 01:06:42.364
   And take the left boot off
        and set it down.


01:06:42.366 --> 01:06:43.631
    I pick up the first one


01:06:43.733 --> 01:06:45.700
  and put it on the same foot
        I just had it on


01:06:45.702 --> 01:06:46.468
       and put on the...


01:06:46.470 --> 01:06:49.471
       So I had basically
         taken them off


01:06:49.473 --> 01:06:50.572
       and put them back
       on the wrong feet


01:06:50.574 --> 01:06:52.307
   and walked outside again.


01:06:55.511 --> 01:06:57.178
   <i> I've been coming down here</i>
           <i> since '99</i>


01:06:57.180 --> 01:06:58.747
       <i> so it's kind of...</i>


01:06:58.749 --> 01:07:00.548
       it's all the same
       to me pretty much.


01:07:00.550 --> 01:07:04.085
           It's gone.
       My memory is gone.


01:07:04.087 --> 01:07:07.088
I remember trying to call my Dad


01:07:07.090 --> 01:07:10.058
    at the same phone number
        I grew up with.


01:07:10.060 --> 01:07:11.192
    I couldn't remember it.


01:07:11.194 --> 01:07:14.329
  I caught myself trying to--


01:07:14.331 --> 01:07:16.131
   It took me over 10 seconds


01:07:16.133 --> 01:07:20.769
  to remember if S came before
  or after T in the alphabet.


01:07:20.771 --> 01:07:23.038
   And that was like a sign.


01:07:23.040 --> 01:07:25.607
        I need to get up
     and away from my desk


01:07:25.708 --> 01:07:26.574
        and get a grip.


01:07:27.643 --> 01:07:28.576
            Ahhhhh.


01:07:30.312 --> 01:07:31.446
            Ahhhhh.


01:07:34.417 --> 01:07:37.619
   I've started saying "Ahhh"
           a lot more


01:07:37.621 --> 01:07:39.187
      than I ever used to
     and it's not something


01:07:39.189 --> 01:07:40.088
         I mean to do.


01:07:40.090 --> 01:07:43.091
    it's just something that
     I use to fill the time


01:07:43.093 --> 01:07:45.760
 where I never did that before
       I came down here.


01:07:45.762 --> 01:07:47.762
        I never, I mean,
       I would say "Ah,"


01:07:47.764 --> 01:07:49.831
     but I would never say
        "Ahhhhhhhhhhh."


01:07:51.500 --> 01:07:53.268
          You ahhhh...


01:07:53.270 --> 01:07:55.236
    I just had a T3 moment.


01:07:55.238 --> 01:07:58.339
        I totally forgot
      my line of thinking.


01:08:01.310 --> 01:08:03.111
        Sorry, what was
     the original question?


01:08:30.873 --> 01:08:34.442
       <i> If there's any way</i>
     <i> to bottle or bring in</i>


01:08:34.444 --> 01:08:36.744
  <i> just the smell of summer...</i>


01:08:36.746 --> 01:08:38.313
    <i> the scent of flowers...</i>


01:08:38.315 --> 01:08:40.215
 <i> and of rain and of green grass</i>


01:08:40.217 --> 01:08:41.282
         <i> and of rivers.</i>


01:08:44.787 --> 01:08:48.423
  <i> The smell of crops and corn</i>


01:08:48.425 --> 01:08:50.225
  <i> and just the smell of dirt.</i>


01:08:51.527 --> 01:08:52.827
 <i> There's no smell of dirt here.</i>


01:08:52.829 --> 01:08:54.762
       <i> It's all volcanic.</i>


01:09:01.637 --> 01:09:02.570
            <i> Oh man.</i>


01:09:03.539 --> 01:09:04.606
        <i> I miss the rain</i>


01:09:04.608 --> 01:09:06.841
   <i> and trees and water and...</i>


01:09:08.277 --> 01:09:11.880
   family and my knuckle-head
            nephews.


01:09:11.882 --> 01:09:13.515
You do miss out on quite a bit.


01:09:14.783 --> 01:09:17.452
  You do make some sacrifices
       coming down here.


01:09:23.826 --> 01:09:28.229
           <i> I probably</i>
   <i> would never repeat winter.</i>


01:09:28.231 --> 01:09:29.797
       <i> The problem is...</i>


01:09:29.799 --> 01:09:30.932
         you never know


01:09:30.934 --> 01:09:32.433
    who you'll end up with.


01:09:40.309 --> 01:09:41.809
        <i> You almost feel</i>
      <i> like you're stuck...</i>


01:09:41.811 --> 01:09:43.378
  <i> stuck in a really small town</i>


01:09:43.380 --> 01:09:45.547
      <i> and there's nothing</i>
       <i> else out there...</i>


01:09:47.349 --> 01:09:48.683
<i>until the sun starts coming out.</i>


01:09:48.685 --> 01:09:50.785
      And then you realize
      where you are again.


01:10:10.906 --> 01:10:13.441
    <i> There's a great feeling</i>
        <i> of anticipation</i>


01:10:13.443 --> 01:10:14.809
      <i> when twilight begins</i>


01:10:14.811 --> 01:10:16.811
   <i> to creep back into the sky</i>
           <i> in August.</i>


01:10:18.547 --> 01:10:20.782
     <i> It's a bit like being</i>
         <i> a child again</i>


01:10:20.784 --> 01:10:22.217
     <i> waiting for Christmas.</i>


01:10:25.788 --> 01:10:28.489
   <i> August is also the coldest</i>
       <i> time of the year.</i>


01:10:30.659 --> 01:10:34.395
      <i> And nacreous clouds</i>
 <i> will start to form a lot more.</i>


01:10:37.299 --> 01:10:39.300
     <i> Although this is part</i>
         <i> of the process</i>


01:10:39.302 --> 01:10:41.869
       <i> that is destroying</i>
        <i> the ozone layer,</i>


01:10:41.871 --> 01:10:43.771
      <i> when the sun finally</i>
         <i> does hit them</i>


01:10:43.773 --> 01:10:45.340
    <i> it can look incredible.</i>


01:10:45.342 --> 01:10:47.575
      <i> like the entire sky</i>
          <i> in on fire.</i>


01:11:21.810 --> 01:11:23.845
 <i> Seeing the sun is always still</i>


01:11:23.847 --> 01:11:25.713
  <i> the most amazing experience.</i>


01:11:25.715 --> 01:11:28.349
         <i> I wait for it</i>
  <i> I wait for it to come back.</i>


01:11:56.378 --> 01:11:59.480
   <i> And then there'll be that</i>
     <i> moment where I see it.</i>


01:11:59.482 --> 01:12:01.482
     And I never know when
  that moment is going to be.


01:12:01.484 --> 01:12:03.451
      But when it happens,


01:12:03.453 --> 01:12:05.720
      I just have to stop
         wherever I am.


01:12:05.722 --> 01:12:07.722
       Stop in my tracks
     and I just look at it.


01:12:07.724 --> 01:12:10.425
     I just want it to fill
     the inside of my head,


01:12:10.427 --> 01:12:12.927
       <i> just let that sun</i>
  <i> come right through my eyes.</i>


01:12:12.929 --> 01:12:14.529
  <i> It's the life-giving thing.</i>


01:12:51.400 --> 01:12:53.401
       Okay, away you go.


01:12:53.403 --> 01:12:55.436
 In this cup is boiling water.


01:12:55.438 --> 01:12:58.039
  It's 40 below zero outside.


01:12:58.041 --> 01:12:59.741
      This is what happens
         when you throw


01:12:59.808 --> 01:13:02.710
       boiling hot water
    into 40 below zero air.


01:13:02.712 --> 01:13:03.945
          Here we go.


01:13:31.073 --> 01:13:34.909
     <i> The Population on base</i>
   <i> suddenly doubles at Winfly</i>


01:13:34.911 --> 01:13:37.111
      <i> and for those of us</i>
     <i> who have wintered over</i>


01:13:37.113 --> 01:13:39.714
     <i> the arrival of a whole</i>
       <i> new crowd of faces</i>


01:13:39.716 --> 01:13:41.482
   <i> can be a bit bewildering.</i>


01:13:50.559 --> 01:13:52.794
      <i> It's kind of crazy.</i>


01:13:52.796 --> 01:13:55.563
     <i> I think people either</i>
      <i> are energized by it</i>


01:13:55.565 --> 01:13:56.864
     <i> or just the opposite.</i>


01:13:56.866 --> 01:13:59.200
     They have energy drawn
           from them


01:13:59.202 --> 01:14:01.436
     and I would tend to be
      one of those people


01:14:01.438 --> 01:14:03.604
 who have energy drawn from me.


01:14:03.606 --> 01:14:06.507
       I'm not a big fan
 of when all the folks come in.


01:14:10.746 --> 01:14:13.147
   <i> For six months you've seen</i>
<i>only the same people every day.</i>


01:14:13.149 --> 01:14:15.016
 <i> There hasn't been anyone new.</i>


01:14:15.018 --> 01:14:18.219
 <i> All of a sudden you've got all</i>
<i>these new people coming through.</i>


01:14:18.221 --> 01:14:21.122
      <i> Kind of this feeling</i>
     <i> of glee and happiness</i>


01:14:21.124 --> 01:14:23.558
      mixed with revulsion
  like, "Aggghhh, stay away!"


01:14:28.630 --> 01:14:30.865
       And I've even seen
   winter-overs kind of hide


01:14:30.867 --> 01:14:33.568
         behind corners
     and kind of look out.


01:14:40.676 --> 01:14:42.910
  <i> We've had a closed community</i>
        <i> over the winter</i>


01:14:42.912 --> 01:14:44.979
   <i> and there's been no germs,</i>
       <i> no one gets sick.</i>


01:14:44.981 --> 01:14:48.583
    <i> But new people come in--</i>
           <i> new germs.</i>


01:14:48.585 --> 01:14:51.152
 <i> They all have all this energy</i>
      <i> and they're orange.</i>


01:14:51.154 --> 01:14:53.521
     <i> I mean we always talk</i>
    <i> about the orange people</i>


01:14:53.523 --> 01:14:54.589
    <i> because they're tanned.</i>


01:14:55.757 --> 01:14:58.926
    You don't really realize
      how pale we all are


01:14:58.928 --> 01:15:00.661
     from lack of sunshine.


01:15:06.935 --> 01:15:08.603
<i>Just walking through the galley,</i>


01:15:08.605 --> 01:15:11.138
    I felt like I was moving
      at this little pace


01:15:11.140 --> 01:15:13.508
       and everyone else
     was rushing around...


01:15:13.510 --> 01:15:14.909
           around me.


01:15:21.817 --> 01:15:25.219
     I was surprised at how
    territorial we all were.


01:15:25.221 --> 01:15:28.556
    I remember getting back
      from the flight line


01:15:28.558 --> 01:15:29.957
 and coming straight to dinner.


01:15:30.859 --> 01:15:33.928
       And I got my tray
          and my plate


01:15:34.763 --> 01:15:37.999
        <i> and I looked up</i>
       <i> and I saw a line.</i>


01:15:38.001 --> 01:15:40.201
       <i> And I was so livid</i>


01:15:40.203 --> 01:15:42.169
  <i> that I had to wait in line.</i>


01:15:43.272 --> 01:15:44.272
     <i> These new people they</i>


01:15:44.274 --> 01:15:45.239
 <i> weren't with the program yet.</i>


01:15:45.241 --> 01:15:46.941
        <i> They didn't know</i>
      <i> what they were doing</i>


01:15:46.943 --> 01:15:48.910
       <i> the whole routine</i>
         <i> was messed up.</i>


01:15:48.912 --> 01:15:49.877
      <i> And I was so livid.</i>


01:15:49.879 --> 01:15:52.680
    <i> I felt like I could have</i>
 <i> stabbed somebody with a fork.</i>


01:15:56.552 --> 01:15:58.119
  <i> And I didn't understand it.</i>


01:15:58.121 --> 01:16:00.087
           <i> I'm like,</i>
      <i> "Why am I so angry?"</i>


01:16:07.829 --> 01:16:08.963
 I couldn't eat in the galley.


01:16:08.965 --> 01:16:10.631
     I went up to my room.


01:16:10.633 --> 01:16:12.300
             And...
     I'm sitting in my room


01:16:12.302 --> 01:16:14.001
      for about 5 minutes
      contemplating about


01:16:14.003 --> 01:16:16.571
      why I was so angry.


01:16:16.573 --> 01:16:18.739
And then I get knocks on my door


01:16:18.741 --> 01:16:21.108
       and it's the rest
       of the Firehouse.


01:16:21.110 --> 01:16:22.643
 "Can we eat in here with you?"


01:16:23.178 --> 01:16:24.612
             Yeah.


01:16:24.614 --> 01:16:25.780
         So we sat down
      and for half an hour


01:16:25.782 --> 01:16:27.181
 we ate our meals watching TV.


01:16:28.216 --> 01:16:30.985
Didn't say a word to each other
     and it was beautiful.


01:16:51.273 --> 01:16:52.340
      <i> The first few days,</i>


01:16:52.342 --> 01:16:53.841
    <i> or maybe the first week,</i>


01:16:53.843 --> 01:16:55.977
  <i> is kind of a culture shock.</i>


01:16:57.112 --> 01:16:59.013
           You know,
      the dynamics change.


01:16:59.015 --> 01:17:00.648
     The noise level rises.


01:17:01.683 --> 01:17:04.885
         <i> But after that</i>
 <i> the new people that come here</i>


01:17:04.887 --> 01:17:07.021
    <i> they have so much energy</i>


01:17:07.023 --> 01:17:09.724
<i>and I find that it brings me up.</i>


01:17:09.825 --> 01:17:12.760
<i>And I actually get more excited</i>
    <i> about getting stuff done</i>


01:17:12.762 --> 01:17:14.662
       <i> and moving around.</i>


01:17:14.664 --> 01:17:15.730
    It kind of wakes me up.


01:17:17.866 --> 01:17:20.301
 Keri, how does it feel to have
 a fresh apple after 6 months?


01:17:25.273 --> 01:17:26.774
         Orange, apple?


01:17:26.776 --> 01:17:27.942
       Why don't you take
       that behind doors?


01:17:27.944 --> 01:17:29.677
<i>I'm sure I'll get one very soon.</i>


01:17:34.349 --> 01:17:36.384
   Be gentle with the banana.


01:18:08.183 --> 01:18:09.684
    <i> I would love to be able</i>


01:18:09.686 --> 01:18:11.152
       <i> to show the people</i>
      <i> who I love the most</i>


01:18:11.154 --> 01:18:12.453
<i>what it looks like down here...</i>


01:18:12.455 --> 01:18:14.155
    what the sky looks like
      down here in winter.


01:18:18.460 --> 01:18:20.194
     <i> Because they're never</i>
        <i> going to see it.</i>


01:18:30.439 --> 01:18:31.906
          <i> It's funny.</i>


01:18:31.908 --> 01:18:34.041
  <i> Right before winter started</i>
    <i> we'd tell these stories</i>


01:18:34.043 --> 01:18:38.079
     <i> about how you'd get T3</i>
        <i> and you get pale</i>


01:18:38.081 --> 01:18:41.315
        <i> and you're just</i>
      <i> emotional sometimes.</i>


01:18:41.317 --> 01:18:43.451
        <i> And these people</i>
    <i> who have never wintered</i>


01:18:43.453 --> 01:18:44.919
       <i> are looking at us</i>
       <i> like we're freaks.</i>


01:18:44.921 --> 01:18:46.253
    <i> Like why would you ever</i>


01:18:46.255 --> 01:18:48.389
      <i> put yourself through</i>
      <i> something like that?</i>


01:18:54.396 --> 01:18:56.163
     <i> And then, at the end,</i>


01:18:57.933 --> 01:18:59.100
<i>we'd look at each other and say,</i>


01:19:00.268 --> 01:19:01.402
      "Winter's the best.


01:19:03.405 --> 01:19:04.505
      It's the greatest."


01:19:14.950 --> 01:19:17.051
       <i> I try and explain</i>
        <i> the experience,</i>


01:19:17.053 --> 01:19:20.121
   <i> the Antarctic experience,</i>
      <i> to people back home,</i>


01:19:20.123 --> 01:19:22.423
         <i> and they love</i>
       <i> hearing about it.</i>


01:19:22.425 --> 01:19:24.225
<i>The stories and what it's like.</i>


01:19:25.160 --> 01:19:28.295
     <i> But, you know that...</i>


01:19:28.297 --> 01:19:30.231
          they just...
    they will never get it.


01:19:30.233 --> 01:19:35.035
 They'll never fully comprehend
   what it's like down here.


01:20:52.547 --> 01:20:55.115
    So if you were to spend
     another year down here


01:20:55.117 --> 01:20:56.984
 <i> what would you do differently?</i>


01:20:58.286 --> 01:21:00.521
<i> Not bring as much stuff.</i>


01:21:13.935 --> 01:21:16.370
I've met some of the best people
       in the world here.


01:21:16.372 --> 01:21:20.207
  And I think a lot of that is
      because of the fact


01:21:20.209 --> 01:21:21.909
that those of us that come here


01:21:21.911 --> 01:21:24.245
       <i> always have a kind</i>
   <i> of a spirit of adventure.</i>


01:21:24.247 --> 01:21:28.282
      <i> And that's something</i>
<i>that kind of binds us together.</i>


01:21:39.494 --> 01:21:41.262
       <i> These might be...</i>


01:21:41.264 --> 01:21:43.230
<i>the golden years of Antarctica.</i>


01:21:47.636 --> 01:21:50.204
           <i> Right now,</i>
 <i> what is being done is science.</i>


01:21:50.206 --> 01:21:51.906
       <i> Right now there's</i>
       <i> a treaty that says</i>


01:21:51.908 --> 01:21:54.441
       <i> you get to be here</i>
         <i> to cooperate,</i>


01:21:54.443 --> 01:21:55.276
        <i> look for peace,</i>


01:21:55.278 --> 01:21:57.344
     <i> and look for knowledge</i>
          <i> for mankind.</i>


01:21:57.346 --> 01:21:59.980
     <i> And I just can't think</i>
        <i> of another place</i>


01:21:59.982 --> 01:22:02.583
  <i> where that's really going on</i>
  <i> so I feel really privileged</i>


01:22:02.585 --> 01:22:05.586
        to be a citizen
    of Antarctica right now.


01:22:05.588 --> 01:22:07.254
      I really really do.


01:22:07.256 --> 01:22:09.957
         <i> And some day,</i>
<i>somebody is going to find a way</i>


01:22:09.959 --> 01:22:10.958
    <i> to get oil commercially.</i>


01:22:10.960 --> 01:22:12.693
         <i> And some day,</i>
   <i> the treaty is going to end</i>


01:22:12.695 --> 01:22:16.063
         <i> And some day,</i>
          <i> you know...</i>


01:22:16.065 --> 01:22:18.132
 <i> I don't know that we'll always</i>
    <i> be able to play as nice</i>


01:22:18.134 --> 01:22:20.167
      <i> as we can right now.</i>


01:22:46.161 --> 01:22:49.263
       <i> You come down here</i>
  <i> out of a sense of adventure.</i>


01:22:51.433 --> 01:22:53.500
        <i> But then it gets</i>
       <i> its hooks in you.</i>


01:22:53.502 --> 01:22:55.235
        <i> and you realize</i>


01:22:55.237 --> 01:22:57.171
     <i> how magic and fragile</i>
           <i> it all is.</i>


01:22:57.173 --> 01:22:59.506
   <i> And if we're not careful,</i>


01:22:59.508 --> 01:23:01.442
  <i> if we're not conscientious,</i>


01:23:01.444 --> 01:23:03.410
    <i> It could all get ruined.</i>


01:23:21.997 --> 01:23:25.065
  <i> Imagine you live in a house.</i>


01:23:25.067 --> 01:23:28.402
   <i> And this is just one room</i>
        <i> in your house...</i>


01:23:28.404 --> 01:23:30.771
          <i> a cold room</i>
      <i> where nobody lives.</i>


01:23:30.773 --> 01:23:33.640
         <i> But it's still</i>
      <i> a room in your house</i>


01:23:33.642 --> 01:23:37.444
      <i> and as such you have</i>
    <i> to care about this room.</i>


01:23:37.446 --> 01:23:40.781
      <i> And you have to know</i>
  <i> about what's going on there.</i>


01:23:53.628 --> 01:23:56.764
<i> There is a good expression</i>
<i><i><i><i>    <i> in the English language:</i>


01:23:56.766 --> 01:23:58.232
         <i> peace of mind.</i>


01:23:58.234 --> 01:23:59.767
       I really like it.


01:23:59.769 --> 01:24:04.038
         Peace of mind
 is a very nice thing to have.


01:24:13.748 --> 01:24:16.216
      <i> The friends you make</i>
        <i> and the memories</i>


01:24:16.218 --> 01:24:19.153
    <i> that you take from here</i>
        <i> last a lifetime.</i>


01:24:19.155 --> 01:24:21.722
     <i> I've met guys who were</i>
     <i> down here 50 years ago</i>


01:24:21.724 --> 01:24:23.290
     who would like nothing
       more in the world


01:24:23.292 --> 01:24:25.492
        than the chance
     to come back again...


01:24:25.494 --> 01:24:27.094
      <i> just one more time.</i>


01:24:32.434 --> 01:24:35.803
 <i> You know you can never really</i>
     <i> call this place home.</i>


01:24:35.805 --> 01:24:39.273
      <i> But at the same time</i>
     <i> there's a familiarity</i>


01:24:39.275 --> 01:24:41.275
      <i> that just builds up.</i>


01:24:44.312 --> 01:24:46.780
    <i> I definitely long for it</i>
         <i> when I'm away.</i>


01:25:33.895 --> 01:25:36.230
         <i> I fully expect</i>
       <i> that my time here</i>


01:25:36.232 --> 01:25:38.398
      <i> is not going to end</i>
          <i> on my terms.</i>


01:25:39.667 --> 01:25:41.502
    <i> The program could change</i>


01:25:41.504 --> 01:25:43.203
      <i> or I might not pass</i>
        <i> the physical...</i>


01:25:44.372 --> 01:25:46.206
  <i> or there might not be a job.</i>


01:25:49.577 --> 01:25:52.279
      <i> No one gets to stay</i>
       <i> here indefinitely.</i>


01:25:58.419 --> 01:26:01.822
    <i> And then the time comes</i>
  <i> when it's you turn to leave</i>


01:26:01.824 --> 01:26:04.158
      <i> and you never really</i>
        <i> do know for sure</i>


01:26:04.160 --> 01:26:05.826
 <i> if you'll ever be back again.</i>


01:27:17.599 --> 01:27:20.801
   <i> One of the things I recall</i>


01:27:20.803 --> 01:27:23.904
         <i> in the process</i>
  <i> of reacclimating to society</i>


01:27:23.906 --> 01:27:26.907
     <i> was a Monday morning.</i>


01:27:26.909 --> 01:27:30.277
       <i> It's probably 8:30</i>
         <i> in the morning</i>


01:27:30.279 --> 01:27:32.713
   <i> and I am stuck in traffic.</i>


01:27:34.015 --> 01:27:36.450
       <i> I remember looking</i>
   <i> at all the cars around me.</i>


01:27:36.452 --> 01:27:39.553
         <i> Everybody's...</i>
 <i> they're in their own little...</i>


01:27:39.555 --> 01:27:42.289
      <i> They're in the grind</i>
         <i> of the world.</i>


01:27:42.291 --> 01:27:45.692
        <i> And I can't help</i>
   <i> but look at everybody else</i>


01:27:45.694 --> 01:27:47.594
          <i> and think...</i>


01:27:47.596 --> 01:27:48.595
        <i> they're cattle.</i>


01:27:48.597 --> 01:27:52.399
     <i> It's just one big herd</i>
<i>moving from point A to point B.</i>


01:27:52.401 --> 01:27:56.603
      <i> and... at that point</i>


01:27:56.605 --> 01:27:58.672
      <i> I wanted to be back</i>
       <i> on the Ice again.</i>


01:28:38.813 --> 01:28:40.347
     <i> It's not until you get</i>
          <i> off the Ice</i>


01:28:40.349 --> 01:28:43.550
  <i> that you realize the absence</i>
  <i> of smell that we have here--</i>


01:28:43.552 --> 01:28:45.485
     <i> the absence of odors.</i>


01:28:45.487 --> 01:28:47.988
           <i> So yeah...</i>


01:28:47.990 --> 01:28:49.923
           <i> you can go</i>
    <i> to the Botanical Gardens</i>


01:28:49.925 --> 01:28:51.892
   <i> for an olfactory overload.</i>


01:29:03.805 --> 01:29:06.840
        <i> I'm going to go</i>
  <i> to the New World Supermarket</i>


01:29:06.842 --> 01:29:09.409
     <i> and I'm going to stand</i>
     <i> in the produce section</i>


01:29:09.411 --> 01:29:11.411
     <i> and just smell the air</i>


01:29:11.413 --> 01:29:12.713
     <i> for about 15 minutes.</i>


01:29:12.715 --> 01:29:17.651
        some really good
      chewy crusty bread,


01:29:17.653 --> 01:29:19.953
     a hunk of really good
          blue cheese,


01:29:19.955 --> 01:29:23.657
      an avocado and some
   red grapes with no seeds.


01:29:23.659 --> 01:29:28.628
And that's what I'm going to eat
       for like 3 meals.


01:29:28.630 --> 01:29:31.665
      There comes a point
         in the winter


01:29:31.667 --> 01:29:33.834
            when...


01:29:33.836 --> 01:29:35.535
     at least us, the guys,


01:29:35.537 --> 01:29:36.603
      us in the Firehouse,


01:29:36.605 --> 01:29:38.472
  we stop talking about women.


01:29:38.474 --> 01:29:41.408
      And we start talking
           about food


01:29:41.410 --> 01:29:43.877
    because it's a much more
      realistic prospect.


01:29:45.813 --> 01:29:47.481
             So...


01:29:47.483 --> 01:29:49.449
     I've narrowed it down.
        I'm going to go


01:29:49.451 --> 01:29:52.119
     and I'm going to have
       steak and lobster.


01:29:53.421 --> 01:29:55.021
     I'm going to splurge.


01:29:55.990 --> 01:29:58.892
 Fresh vegetables with flavor.


01:29:58.894 --> 01:30:03.630
A bean burrito from Taco Bell.


01:30:03.632 --> 01:30:04.698
          <i> Dark bread.</i>


01:30:05.833 --> 01:30:06.900
            Avocado.


01:30:09.137 --> 01:30:10.437
          Cauliflower.


01:30:10.439 --> 01:30:12.806
      A bowl of cornflakes
         with real milk


01:30:12.808 --> 01:30:14.908
      and sliced bananas.


01:30:14.910 --> 01:30:18.145
 Eggs Benedict at the Boulevard
        in New Zealand.


01:30:18.147 --> 01:30:21.715
    Anything in Christchurch
        is always good.


01:30:21.816 --> 01:30:23.183
  Anything non-institutional.


01:30:25.019 --> 01:30:28.622
 When I get back to New Zealand
  the first thing I long to do


01:30:28.624 --> 01:30:31.558
 well first, first thing is go
  through the Botanic Gardens


01:30:31.560 --> 01:30:34.728
    and just touch the grass
     and smell the flowers.


01:30:34.730 --> 01:30:36.863
     But then I try to get
          to the ocean


01:30:36.865 --> 01:30:37.898
  to see that motion I guess.


01:30:37.900 --> 01:30:39.466
       <i> You're standing on</i>
         <i> the ocean now.</i>


01:30:39.468 --> 01:30:40.100
            Exactly.


01:30:40.102 --> 01:30:42.536
    That's what's so funny.
    And I'm a mountain girl,


01:30:42.538 --> 01:30:44.137
       so it's never been
         a draw before.


01:30:47.942 --> 01:30:49.976
    <i> Walk barefoot in grass.</i>


01:30:54.048 --> 01:30:56.817
 <i> I'm going to fly straight home</i>
      <i> to Washington State.</i>


01:30:56.819 --> 01:31:00.520
   And I'm going to fly-fish
my brains out for about 3 weeks


01:31:00.522 --> 01:31:02.055
going for salmon and steel head.


01:31:02.057 --> 01:31:04.925
        And when I puke,
 I think that's when I'll stop.


01:31:06.194 --> 01:31:08.695
  I really like going to sleep
         in my own bed.


01:31:08.697 --> 01:31:11.064
        I really like--
            Oh rain.


01:31:11.066 --> 01:31:12.999
     Just hearing the rain
         and seeing it


01:31:13.001 --> 01:31:15.502
       feeling it again.
           Wonderful


01:31:16.170 --> 01:31:18.472
    <i> I plan on doing nothing.</i>


01:31:18.474 --> 01:31:20.974
I hope it rains at least one day
   while I'm in Christchurch,


01:31:20.976 --> 01:31:22.843
         just so I can
   wander around in the rain.


01:31:22.845 --> 01:31:23.643
         I'd love that.


01:31:23.645 --> 01:31:26.847
         I hope it's--
       I want some rain.


01:31:30.184 --> 01:31:32.586
      Have a decent sleep.


01:31:33.521 --> 01:31:35.755
      Have a decent sleep
        for a few days.


01:31:36.891 --> 01:31:38.625
         I don't know.


01:31:39.760 --> 01:31:42.128
    Check into a hotel room
        and take a bath.


01:31:55.710 --> 01:31:57.244
     My brain is freezing.


01:31:58.713 --> 01:31:59.713
         Let me think.


01:31:59.715 --> 01:32:02.549
I think my brain is freezing now
       and I can't think.


01:32:04.919 --> 01:32:06.686
      Skip that question.

